# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit anything that carries the licensed SpinRite binaries, real
# hardware identifiers, or host/session state.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# VM disk images. SRDOS-disk001.vdi holds the owner's licensed SpinRite.
*.vdi
*.vhd
*.qcow2

# Raw physical-disk pointers. Filenames encode drive model + serial, and the
# descriptors bake in a specific host's device nodes. spinrite-attach.sh
# recreates these on every run.
*.vmdk

# Bootable utility images (SpinRite.img, FreeDOS install media, ISOs).
*.img
*.iso

# Backup tarballs produced by bin/spinrite-backup.sh. These intentionally
# contain the VDI, the real tracker CSV and Claude memory files.
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
spinrite-backups/

# The real run tracker: drive serials and computer service tags.
# Ship examples/spinrite-tracker.example.csv instead.
spinrite-tracker.csv

# Claude Code host state: session history, settings, and .credentials.json.
.claude/
.claude.json

# VirtualBox host/session leftovers
*.vbox-prev
Logs/
VBox.log*

# Editor / OS noise
*~
*.swp
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
